{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1114229-rite-of-the-fading-wolf-new-rite","id":1114229,"title":"Rite of the Fading Wolf (New Rite)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-10T11:56:49-07:00","id":1114229,"title":"Rite of the Fading Wolf (New Rite)","content":"Since there is an ongoing discussion about the Skin Dancers, I decided to develop an alternative to their Rite and share it with the community. If you wish, feel free to adapt it, ignore it, or use it, it is freely given. I would not mind though if you all shared your opinions about the Rite, as I know that it could potentially change the dynamics of Garou-Kinfolk relations in WtA.<br /> <br /> <b>Rite of the Fading Wolf (Level Five Mystic Rite)</b><br /> <br /> While the Garou attempt to find a place for all of the Garou, some Garou find that the burden of being Garou becomes too great. Whether it is because of the social stigma of being Metis, the intensity of possessing Rage, the fatigue that comes with old age, or the disability that comes with battle scars, there are always Garou who desire to give up their Garou nature. While some of them go insane or some of them become Ronin, the majority of them consent to this rite to transfer their Garou nature onto a human child or a wolf cub. While it is known by different names, the majority of the Fera breeds developed a similar rite for their members who wished to pass on the burden of their existence to the next generation.<br /> <br /> When a Garou willing participates in this rite, without any compulsions, inducements, or threats, this rite transfers their Garou nature onto a Human Kinfolk child of their Tribe that is less than thirteen moons old or a Wolf Kinfolk cub of their Tribe that is less than three moons old. In the case of a Human Kinfolk child of their Tribe, the child will experience their First Change thirteen times thirteen moons after the performance of the ritual. In the case of a Wolf Kinfolk cub of their Tribe, the cub will experience their First Change three times thirteen moons after the performance of the ritual. In either case, the Tribe will raise the child or cub with the knowledge that they will become one of the Garou and with the expectation of great things from the child or the cub.<br /> <br /> The effect of the ritual on the Garou sacrificing their Garou nature is dramatic. In the case of Homid Garou, they become Human Kinfolk. In the case of Lupus Garou, they become Wolf Kinfolk. In the case of Metis Garou, they divide into two entities, one Homid Kinfolk and one Wolf Kinfolk, each without the Metis Disability (or the resulting sterility), and each with equivalent capabilities; though they diverge as their life experiences diverge.<br /> <br /> Whether they become Human Kinfolk and/or Lupus Kinfolk, they sacrifice their Rank and any permanent Renown above the fifth rank. In addition, they sacrifice their Rage and any permanent Gnosis above the third rank. They retain any level one Gifts that do not require Rage, but they sacrifice any level one Gifts that require Rage and any Gifts above the first level. They retain knowledge of any Rites but, while they may teach the Rites that they know, they are incapable of performing any Rites other than Minor Rites. In the majority of the Tribes, their Tribe accords the Kinfolk formed from former Garou with great respect because they sacrificed their Garou nature so that one of the Kinfolk could become one of the Garou.<br /> <br /> <b>System</b>: The ritemaster must first successfully summon an Avatar of the Totem of the Tribe of the Garou sacrificing their Garou nature and the cub or child so that the Garou in question may explain the reason why he or she is sacrificing their nature. If the ritemaster successfully performs the rite, the Avatar of the Totem agrees to the sacrifice and, touching both the Garou and the child or cub, transfers the Garou nature from one to the other, transforming the sacrificing Garou into Human Kinfolk and/or Wolf Kinfolk and the child or cub into a future Garou. The influence of the Avatar of the Totem in the transfer of the Garou nature means that the child or cub effectively becomes a child of the Avatar of the Totem. The child or cub gains one level of Spirit Heritage per success gained by the ritemaster when he or she performs the rite, up to a maximum of five levels, which overrides any other form of Spirit Heritage that they may have otherwise possessed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T14:20:57-07:00","id":1114277,"title":"","content":"This Rite has zero price to it. It doesn't just change relationships between Garou and Kin, it changes the whole dynamic of the game. There's no reason to ever not use this Rite. A Garou has suffered one too many Battle Scars and just can't function well even as a fighter any more? Why not pass their Garou status on? Why not pressure Metis to undergo the Rite as much as possible? Etc. <br /> <br /> One of the things about the Skin Dancers, is that it takes five Garou pelts for every Skin Dancer you make. Even if five Garou wanted to give up their status for someone that desires it to back up the mantle, you'd have to have all of them together at the same time and all that. A one-to-one ratio means there's not even that as a reason to not use this Rite.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T14:52:21-07:00","id":1114289,"title":"","content":"I agree with Heavy Arms, this is just a better version of Rite of Sacred Rebirth. The Rite already says that 5 Garou can willingly give their pelts to fuel the ritual. Doing so allows the new shifter not to acquire taint, so this rite is not necessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T22:34:40-07:00","id":1114446,"title":"","content":"I agree with 'Arms.<br /> <br /> This Rite violates the Garou society, kin-Garou relationship, demography, and - in my vievpoint - the will of Gaia.<br /> This Rite could lend the Garou false hope and a quick exit from a tortured existence (They are not suppesed to be furry superheroes). Every cub (with a right tutor) could whine a little, and pass their sacred role to a dupe.<br /> They wouldn't be hard pressed to maintain relations and repopulate. They could more easily fall into Harano (without a special role). Black Furies could force the males to pass over their beeing to a women, depriving other tribes of fresh male blood. The Silver Fangs could &quot;cleanse&quot; their blood with drastic measures. Red Talons could hunt homids and awake wolves. They...<br /> <br /> If this Rite would work, it would be the work of the Wyrm. But this could be the good story to tell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T10:39:14-07:00","id":1115582,"title":"","content":"This rite... would basically eliminate the &quot;old age&quot; illness of Garou: Harano, where they go all distressed and depressed before they waste away. I would not exactly oppose it... but up the price... and make it as rare as... That rite that only ONE Nuwisha on earth knows at any time: It is a such great secret.<br /> <br /> *The garou giving up their status will die in the ritual, no matter the further outcome<br /> *The Garou that performed the rite forgets how it is performed.<br /> *The Totem of the tribe has to agree the transfer - some of them never do!<br /> *If the child is found unworthy by the Totem, it dies, even if the Totem agreed to the transfer itself.<br /> *Becoming a Garou this way grants at least one of the battlescars of the donor without gaining the associated renown.<br /> <br /> And... I would tag a price to daring to <i>learn</i> the rite...<br /> <br /> <br /> All in all: there is that one legendary cart... that one that can bring back heroes for the price of the life of some women. Where the garou that lead the search for 12 or such filled the ranks to get ONE back. This rite idea should be worked on to fit that picture of an epic plot device you shouldn't touch lightly for its price.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9729-hira-akigi","name":"Hira Akigi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}